</md></sn><sn><md>#### Critical Values Derived from Dose-Response Data

From dose-response data, toxicologists derive several critical values:

| Value | Definition |
|-------|------------|
| **ED50** | The dose that produces the **desired effect** in 50% of the test population |
| **LD50** | The dose **lethal** to 50% of the test population |

**Notes on LD50:**
- Usually expressed in **milligrams of chemical per kilogram of body weight (mg/kg)**
- A chemical with a **small LD50** (e.g., 5 mg/kg) is considered **very highly toxic**</md></sn>